From 6384bf16147e13efaa71f882d1e33ffc2bced6dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:53:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 217/294] gallium/pvr: assemble the draw stream the captured
 working draw has

The probe's render submission now has the same shape as the capture: a PPP state block (TA state in
memory, named by PPP_STATE_UPDATE), the full VDM vertex state, an index list, a terminate block and
STREAM_TERMINATE. No PDS state updates, no standalone launchers - those were stand-ins from
milestone 1 and the capture shows they are not how a draw is expressed.

- USC and PDS programs are placed at chosen addresses in their heaps and named by heap-relative
  offsets, which is what the hardware state takes (the capture's decoded values are absolute only
  because the dump tool adds the heap base back): VS/FS code in the USC heap, the attribute
  program's code+data and the fragment stage's kick program in the PDS heap.
- The TA state block carries the capture's 25 words: header presence, ISPCTL + both face words + DBSC,
  the five PDS words, region clip, viewport, wclamp, output select (vtxsize = the VS's 5 varying
  dwords), varying counts, PPP ctrl and stream out. The probe checks all 20 state-determined words
  against the capture byte for byte; the other five are this pipeline's own PDS addresses/sizes.
- The terminate block and the fragment kick program complete the chain: the FS is named by
  TA_STATE_PDS_SHADERBASE + SIZEINFO, not by a DDM PDS update.

Two ownership bugs found while wiring it, both silent:

- pco_shader keeps a pointer to the NIR it was built from, so callers that free the NIR corrupt the
  heap at some later, unrelated allocation. pvr_shader_compile_data now ralloc_steals it, the rule
  the Vulkan driver's build_shader uses.
- The vertex maps must be allocated AFTER pco_lower_nir: lowering adds the gl_PointSize output, and a
  map built earlier misses it (the translator then writes it to register 0). The captured draw's
  5 output dwords are exactly position + point size.

Verification (DRM noop shim, no GPU): probe exits 0, ALL PASS; TA block matches the captured draw;
VDM state reproduces the captured dwords; PDS/TA/USC offsets are heap-relative. The stream has not
executed on hardware yet - that is the next step.
